# The self-hosted crates' Rust is **generated** from the `.sdx` beside it.
#
# `crates/redox-ast/sdx/**` and `crates/redox-fmt/sdx/**` are the source; the
# `.rs` under each crate's `src/` is written by `redox build` and committed,
# because the committed output *is* this project's previous-version compiler
# (doc 02 §4.8) — stored as reviewable Rust rather than as a prebuilt binary,
# which is the thing rustc, Go, Zig and OCaml all have to download or check in
# as a blob and cannot read.
#
# **No longer committed at all**, since plan 72 leaf 5: these trees are in
# `.gitignore` and `./bootstrap.sh` regenerates them from `seed/redox1.wasm`.
#
# The rules below are kept rather than deleted because they are still correct
# and still cheap. `git add -f` on one of these files is a thing a person does
# while debugging a generation, and if it happens the attributes are what stop
# ~32,000 lines of authorless output from arriving as a reviewable diff.
#
# Plan 70 added them when the trees *were* committed, with `linguist-generated`
# to keep them out of the language statistics and `-diff` to collapse a
# regeneration to one line.

# The one binary this repository tracks — plan 72 leaf 3, and `seed/SEED.md`
# is its provenance. Marked binary so git never attempts a textual diff or a
# line-ending conversion on it, and `linguist-generated` so it stays out of the
# language statistics: it is a compiled artifact of this repository's own Rust,
# not a vendored dependency.
seed/redox1.wasm binary linguist-generated=true

crates/redox-ast/src/**/*.rs linguist-generated=true -diff
crates/redox-fmt/src/**/*.rs linguist-generated=true -diff
